# IN THE ROUTER POOLS (prod `box-a` in box-c-prod, dev `box-a-dev` in box-c-dev), serving beside box-b (box-c stopped, the fallback),
# on the NVIDIA megakernel: tools/args/stack-b300-box-a-mk2.args + env-box-a-mk2.txt (ENV_SEED, config X') on
# SGLANG_TREE=/workspace/mk29/sglang in VENV=/opt/sglang-mk29, watched by hangwatch.py (--service --on-hang kill)
# beside watchdog.sh. Record: qa/prod-merge-20261030/raw/gate/NOTES.md (config X' on prod's tip, its gate and way
# back), before it qa/box-a-megakernel-20261029/raw/box-a-return/NOTES.md (config X, and its rollback recipe);
# the retired-era record is fleet-history/box-a/README.md. BOX_IP/SSH_PORT/APP_PORT_EXT are re-read
# from `hostctl show instance` at a start.
# box-a — 4× B300 on a rented host, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (L3a) under SGLang: the second,
# differently-named box after box-c (box-c/README.md, "Standing up a second, differently-named box"), cut from
# boxes/box-c.env with only the box-identifying keys and the 4× B300 shape changed. It serves the
# same build box-c served (SERVE_BUILD/MODEL_DIR/SERVED_MODEL) on the megakernel tree /workspace/mk29/sglang @ 9a9ede7ae018
# (our SGLang fork prod, detached; before it 4943d6ed906a, the way back) with tools/args/stack-b300-box-a-mk2.args + tools/args/env-box-a-mk2.txt (config X'
# = config X + box-c's host-alloc threads, write_through_selective, exact decoder trim, cached image refs). Way back:
# config X, tools/args/stack-b300-box-a-mk.args + tools/args/env-box-a-mk.txt on 9ec65dacaf52 (branch box-a-mk-latest,
# qa/box-a-megakernel-20261029/), same VENV/CACHE; before it the final, tools/args/stack-b300-box-a.args + tools/args/env-box-a-w1.txt
# on the box-e tree's checkout (box-e-up) at the fork's prod 819756d4 (box-a-ship1 + upstream #46700's SWA tombstone
# clamp) with VENV=/opt/sglang-box-e, CACHE=/workspace/cache-box-a (FORK_TREE's comment), the stack its ship-1 run
# shipped (qa/box-a-ship1-20261027/README.md); further back box-a-ship1 ace628a0, then v1-b300-box-a.args +
# env-box-a.txt on prod-20261026 fd3545a46b53df3b01a4ed1b01a460d29f442385 (qa/box-a-tuning-20261026/README.md).
# Every script in ../ sources this through lib.sh (BOX=box-a). No secrets here:
# they live in ENV_FILE on the dev box and in /etc/environment on the box.
BOX=box-a
BOX_IP="<BOX_IP>"           # instance <INSTANCE_ID> (offer <OFFER_ID>, machine <MACHINE_ID>): its public_ipaddr
SSH_PORT="<SSH_PORT>"                 # instance <INSTANCE_ID>'s DIRECT 22/tcp host mapping (container 22 -> <BOX_IP>:<SSH_PORT>). Not 37336: that is the provider's listed ssh_port, the ssh7.the provider proxy
SSH_KEY="~/.ssh/<SSH_KEY>"   # the key a SANDBOXED worker can read and authenticate with (no passphrase; box-c's own SSH_KEY). The the provider ACCOUNT key (<EMAIL>, ~/.ssh/id_rsa) -- what a create injects -- is passphrase-protected, so a sandboxed ssh with BatchMode=yes cannot use it; this key works only once it is in the box's /root/.ssh/authorized_keys (`hostctl attach ssh <INSTANCE_ID> ~/.ssh/<SSH_KEY>.pub`, as #17 did for box-c)
APP_PORT_EXT="<APP_PORT_EXT>"             # instance <INSTANCE_ID>'s 8001/tcp host mapping (DOOR_PORT's external port): the router dials https://box-a.<DOMAIN>:<APP_PORT_EXT>
DOOR_PORT=8001                # container port Caddy listens on (the mapped one)
ENGINE_PORT=8002              # SGLang, loopback only
HOSTNAME="box-a.<DOMAIN>"   # the name the door serves; its DNS record points at BOX_IP
CF_ZONE="<DOMAIN>"
TLS_ALLOW="<ALLOW_CIDR> 127.0.0.1/32 ::1/128"   # the door's source-IP allowlist (space-separated CIDRs, QUOTED: lib.sh sources this file): stage.sh writes it into caddy.env on every stage and the door renders it as the Caddyfile's @allowed matcher, everyone else 403. Required while this file has a door: stage.sh refuses to write an open caddy.env without it (TLS_ALLOW_ANY=1 is the explicit opt-out)
CADDY_EXPECT_SHA256=22e29521abb1ce00c030192f3c6f9126ecd84c431a672872d04095c1b1c15aba   # the front door's Caddy binary of record, by sha256: stock v2.11.7 + caddy-dns/cloudflare v0.2.4, go1.26.4 (caddyserver.com's build server) -- what this box serves today. The staged binary is pinned by this value (tools/caddy-h2/README.md). The front-door deploy item (#869) flips this to the patched b843f7bb8c43bae5b8b1b2631993a26c8dfeda1dabaa865bc7fda4a2e8d4d884 (tools/caddy-h2/, the h2 receive windows 16/8 MiB) only after this box's binary swap
SERVE_BUILD=1017-l3a   # edited as a pair with MODEL_DIR: names the build this box serves (box-c's)
MODEL_DIR="<MODEL_PATH>"   # the L3a repack sglang serve loads, the same path and build as box-c's MODEL_DIR. Literal, never a reference: boxenv.py's KEY=VALUE parser cannot expand one. stage.sh writes it into serve-model.env, which relaunch.sh and a re-create's first boot read
STOCK_DIR=/workspace/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017   # the onstart's hf-download target on a re-create (the stock 1017 checkpoint, 48 shards) and the source graft-apply.sh rebuilds MODEL_DIR from; box-a's first MODEL_DIR is a copy of box-c's repack, so this path may be absent on the box until a re-create. Read by the onstart only while ONSTART_MODEL_SOURCE is stock
ONSTART_MODEL_SOURCE=copied   # build-onstart.sh: box-a serves a repack COPIED from box-c, so its onstart downloads nothing and gates the engine on MODEL_DIR's 48 shards + index/config/tokenizer AND MODEL_READY_MARKER (the stock render would pull 476 GiB into STOCK_DIR on every restart). sshd, the grant and Caddy come up before that gate. A re-create that should rebuild from a stock download instead drops this line and MODEL_READY_MARKER
MODEL_READY_MARKER="<MODEL_READY_MARKER>"   # written by the copy's own `sha256sum -c` against xfer-logs/expected.sha256 once every shard verified; the copy pre-sizes its shards, so a file count alone proves nothing mid-copy
ONSTART_GRANT_FILE=/workspace/tools/authorized_keys2.box-a-kv   # the router tunnel's key (box-a-kv), staged on the box by hand; every boot restores /root/.ssh/authorized_keys2 from it (the provider's injector writes only authorized_keys)
HANGWATCH_CMD="python3 /workspace/mk29/harness/hangwatch.py --service --on-hang kill --out /workspace/mk29/watch/serving --dump-signal none"   # build-onstart.sh (autopool B1): every boot starts the hang watcher after the engine launch (relaunch.sh starts the watchdog); a running copy (same script, same --out) is kept; it holds its own BOOT grace while the engine loads. --dump-signal none: the USR2 catcher in our ranks is LLVM (Triton) with SA_RESETHAND, so the default USR2 stack dump kills the rank (qa/sglang-takes-20261104/merge-b300/NOTES.md, M1/M1b); build-onstart.sh refuses a knob that leaves --dump-signal to the default
FREEZEGC_CMD="bash /workspace/tools/freeze-gc-timer.sh --interval-s 300"   # the recurring POST /freeze_gc (tools/freeze-gc-timer.sh, loopback, content-free log /workspace/freezegc/timer.log), as box-b runs it (#958): the schedulers' >1 s eviction passes were gen2 GC (qa/eviction-stall-20261105/NOTES.md). Started on every boot by the onstart's FREEZEGC block, after the HANGWATCH block: build-onstart.sh renders this key (#960, onstart.sh.tmpl `#@freezegc{`, tests/onstart-freezegc.test.sh). The box's /root/onstart.sh still carries the block #959 hand-added (backup /root/onstart.sh.pre-m959; no boot was run to prove it), equal to the render on every non-comment line, so autopool/install-onstart.sh would change only its comments. setsid gives it its own session and process group, so neither a watchdog relaunch (its pkill patterns are sglang serv[e] / sglang:[:], watchdog.sh) nor a hangwatch kill (the serve process's own group or its descendants, hangwatch.py on_hang_kill) should reach it: read from the code and the process table, never a forced relaunch or kill (qa/eviction-stall-20261105/rolls-box-a/NOTES.md "Freeze timer"); flock on /workspace/freezegc/timer.lock keeps one copy. A re-created instance's onstart starts it too, once stage.sh has put tools/freeze-gc-timer.sh at /workspace/tools (a missing script prints FREEZEGC-MISSING and the boot goes on; start it by hand then, `setsid nohup <this command> >> /workspace/freezegc/nohup.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &`). Stop: touch /workspace/freezegc/stop
SERVED_MODEL=DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
CACHE=/workspace/cache-mk29   # XDG_CACHE_HOME for the megakernel tree on this box (env-box-a-mk.txt sets the same); the box-e-up tree's is /workspace/cache-box-a (the rollback's): one cache dir per tree on a box, never shared (boxes/box-c.env's CACHE line says why)
TOOLS_REMOTE=/workspace/tools # where stage.sh puts this tool set on the box
CERT_PUSH_PUBKEY="<SSH_PUBKEY>"   # the operator host's /root/.ssh/cert-push_ed25519 (public half, config not a secret); on box-a the forced line is added by hand (no re-stage on box-a)
SGLANG_TREE=/workspace/mk29/sglang   # the megakernel checkout at FORK_TREE, the editable sglang of VENV (the rollback's is /workspace/box-e-up at 819756d4). ENV_SEED below picks the env. Its HEAD is detached at FORK_TREE (prod's tip, fetched from the fork; the branch box-a-mk-latest stays at the rollback's 9ec65dacaf): restart.sh/cutover.sh never stage
ENV_SEED=env-box-a-mk3.txt   # the env seed stage.sh (first boot), restart.sh and cutover.sh (`default`) copy to sglang-env.txt, over SGLANG_TREE's tree-name pick. env-box-a-mk3.txt (#959) is env-box-a-mk2.txt + PYTHONPATH=/workspace/site-mk3 (args/site-mk3/sitecustomize.py, installed there BY HAND -- nothing stages it, and a missing dir boots silently without it: the install line is env-box-a-mk3.txt's header; PR_SET_PTRACER_ANY so py-spy attaches to a live rank, and a gen2-GC > 0.1 s timer to the serve log + /workspace/gclog/<pid>.log; content-free; the way back is env-box-a-mk2.txt). env-box-a-mk2.txt is env-box-a-mk.txt + SGLANG_HICACHE_HOST_PARALLEL_ALLOC_THREADS=32, SGLANG_DSV4_EXACT_DECODER_TRIM=1, SGLANG_MM_CACHED_REFS=1, SGLANG_MM_CACHED_REFS_EMBEDDING_CACHE=0 (its header), paired with args/stack-b300-box-a-mk2.args; config X's seed (the way back) env-box-a-mk.txt is env-box-a-w1.txt with the megakernel's deltas (engram layout per_rank, SGLANG_SPEC_TP_SYNC, PATH/XDG_CACHE_HOME onto the mk29 venv/cache) + the TP probe (SGLANG_MK_TP_PROBE=1, EVERY=100, ASSERT=1). The rollback's seed is env-box-a-w1.txt (env-box-a.txt + TRITON_PRINT_AUTOTUNING=1, the ship-1 FINAL env). A bare file name under tools/args/ -- a path, or anything not env-*.txt, refuses
VENV=/opt/sglang-mk29   # the megakernel venv on this box: an editable install of /workspace/mk29/sglang/python plus the plugin /workspace/mk29/sgl-nvidia-mega (54b4289 + the B300 patch, editable); relaunch.sh puts $VENV/bin first on PATH. The rollback's is /opt/sglang-box-e (tools/args/image-box-e.freeze.txt + an editable /workspace/box-e-up/python, qa/box-e-venv/README.md). Neither exists in a fresh container of the image: a re-create builds them before the first restart
# The engine's runtime gate files, materialized by stage.sh on every stage (1 creates the file under
# TOOLS_REMOTE, 0 removes it; the path is the one sglang-env.txt's SGLANG_SBR_*_GATE_FILE key names), set to
# box-c's live state: box-a's first boot ran tool-strict level 0 because tool-strict.on was a hand step nobody took.
TOOL_STRICT=1                  # /workspace/tools/tool-strict.on: SGLANG_TOOL_STRICT_LEVEL=1 applies, as on box-c
SBR_SCHEMA_MEMO=1              # /workspace/tools/sbr-schema-memo.gate: schema memo on, as on box-c
SBR_UNFINISHED_REUSE=1         # /workspace/tools/sbr-unfinished-reuse.gate: unfinished-turn reuse on, as on box-c
SBR_PHASE_TIMING=0             # /workspace/tools/sbr-phase-timing.gate: phase timing closed, as on box-c
# The watchdog's cold-boot budget (watchdog.sh): box-a's first boot took 27 min (~10 min of it FlashInfer
# autotune); the default 2700 s covers it, set here so the figure this box needs is written down.
WATCHDOG_BOOT_GRACE=2700
# Scheduler CPU pinning (relaunch.sh, after /health): TP0..TP3's scheduler processes, every thread, one
# core each (`taskset -a -pc`). #385 measured it live on this box, three alternations: C1 6.00-6.36
# ms/step and 508-538 tok/s pinned vs 6.51-6.96 ms and 405-505 tok/s unpinned (qa/box-a-ship1-20261027/README.md
# "CPU"). Unset it to boot unpinned. 16 17 32 33 are node-0 turbo cores on this machine (#696: ~4600 MHz busy,
# most other cores held at 2300; C1 5.4 vs 7.1 ms/step on 2 4 6 8; README "Turbo cores"): after any host event
# (host turbo/priority config change, instance moved) re-check each with a 2 s pinned spin, busy MHz not idle.
SCHED_CPU_PIN="16 17 32 33"
INSTANCE_ID="<INSTANCE_ID>"         # created 2026-10-26 from offer <OFFER_ID>, machine <MACHINE_ID>; label box-a-dsv41-b300
# The box's GPU SHAPE, read by offer-search.sh. These three set, it searches this box's own 4× B300 shape
# rather than falling back to box-g's book.
GPU_NAME=B300             # the GPU name the search and the label are built from
NUM_GPUS=4                # the TP4 target (stack-b300-box-a.args: --tp-size 4 --ep-size 4)
DISK_GB=1500              # host-disk floor AND `create --disk` (what <INSTANCE_ID> was created with): the ~510 GB repack, plus a re-create's ~510 GB stock download that graft-apply.sh hardlinks the repack from, plus caches. the provider disk cannot be resized after create
# INSTANCE_LABEL is deliberately unset: offer-search.sh derives ${BOX}-dsv41-${GPU_NAME} -> box-a-dsv41-b300, the label <INSTANCE_ID> carries
ENV_FILE="<HOME>/env/box-a.env"   # dev box: VLLM_API_KEY (origin bearer -- a fresh one, never box-c's), HF_TOKEN (stock checkpoint download). This box's OWN file, never tracked
FORK_REPO=sgl-project/sglang       # the PUBLIC upstream this fork tracks, as a bare owner/repo slug ONLY (boxes/box-c.env's FORK_REPO line)
FORK_BRANCH=prod   # the our SGLang fork branch FORK_TREE is the head of: prod's tip 163591d9fc (CAND-FIX committed, FORK_TREE below). Before it 9a9ede7ae0 (4943d6ed90 + CI-only 60ba30cf99 + sweep b's picks #47627 inert, #43110, #47521, #46720; qa/sglang-takes-20261031/NOTES.md). Before it 4943d6ed90 (the merge of box-a-mk-latest into prod 0ab213b25a + sbr test fixes + 2 redaction gaps + upstream picks #46645, #38565, #47149). Config X's line (the way back): FORK_BRANCH=box-a-mk-latest FORK_TREE=9ec65dacaf5269d412a4098dd905debe3e05ed30, the side branch's head (not on prod then). The final's line (FORK_BRANCH=prod FORK_TREE=819756d4..., below) was: the fork branch FORK_TREE is the head of: our SGLang fork's prod, its default branch, fast-forwarded 452f2438 -> 819756d4 (CHANGELOG 2026-10-28), so prod's head IS the tree this box serves. 819756d4 = box-a-ship1 ace628a0 (prod 452f2438 + box-e-img-order 35e6d667 + box-e-swa-interior-evict 9e295882, the ship-1 FINAL tree) + upstream e7c55f69, sgl-project/sglang#46700's SWA tombstone clamp; branch box-a-ship1-46700 heads the same commit. stage.sh's fork fetch pulls it, and bringup.sh falls back to fork/$FORK_BRANCH when FORK_TREE is empty. fork-sync.sh refuses --push to prod (and to any branch holding FORK_TREE), so this served line is never rebased in place: a new tree for this box is a fast-forward of prod or a new branch, with FORK_BRANCH and FORK_TREE moved here in the same change
FORK_TREE=163591d9fcf8c9e9bcaffa2fcc79242fb772fc72   # the COMMIT this box SERVES: prod's tip, CAND-FIX committed = sweep-c ad34bd2e96 + b268b87e98 (hicache: keep the Full host eviction heap across calls) + its test. box-a's engine booted the identical bytes as ad34bd2e96 + the same two changes `git apply`d, uncommitted (#834, qa/sglang-takes-20261104/b300/NOTES.md "What booted"); #915 moved SGLANG_TREE onto the commit with `git reset -q 163591d9fc` (HEAD and index only, no file written: python/ and the untracked test file were already the commit's bytes), so its HEAD is FORK_TREE and clean, and a restart's `--tree 163591d9fc` checkout has nothing to trip on (qa/sglang-takes-20261104/stage-20261104/README.md). Rollback: ROLLBACK_TREES in order (9a9ede7ae0, qa/sglang-takes-20261031/ROLL-box-a.md; then 4943d6ed90, prod before sweep b's picks, qa/prod-merge-20261030/raw/gate/NOTES.md), same branch/args/env/paths. Further back: FORK_BRANCH=box-a-mk-latest FORK_TREE=9ec65dacaf5269d412a4098dd905debe3e05ed30 (config X, qa/box-a-megakernel-20261029/raw/build-latest/tree-ff.md) with stack-b300-box-a-mk.args + env-box-a-mk.txt, same SGLANG_TREE/VENV/CACHE. X lacks upstream #38565 (deterministic top-p/top-k renorm at TP>1) and does not broadcast DSpark's sampled accept (-dspark-accept-sample), the path #38565 shows hanging NCCL: roll back to X only while box-a takes no top_p<1 / top_k traffic (out of the pools, or greedy/top_p 1.0 tests); for traffic, take X with the S6b syncsample plugin build (qa/box-a-megakernel-20261029/args/mk-syncsample.*, SGLANG_SPEC_TP_SYNC=rng; the stock plugin refuses rng alone at startup). Further back: FORK_BRANCH=prod FORK_TREE=819756d4632e9a1f07234e97c11137a591a79193 at SGLANG_TREE=/workspace/box-e-up, VENV=/opt/sglang-box-e, CACHE=/workspace/cache-box-a, ENV_SEED=env-box-a-w1.txt with tools/args/stack-b300-box-a.args, which was: our SGLang fork prod's head (ace628a0 + the #46700 fix), checked out at SGLANG_TREE, on the same stack-b300-box-a.args + env-box-a-w1.txt as before. A commit sha, never a tree object sha (bringup.sh verifies `git rev-parse --verify $FORK_TREE^{commit}` on the box). Rollback: FORK_BRANCH=box-a-ship1 FORK_TREE=ace628a0e9d26a79003195775d171a8a9c7ac0c7 (the ship-1 FINAL tree, qa/box-a-ship1-20261027/README.md), same args/env; further back fd3545a46b53df3b01a4ed1b01a460d29f442385 (prod-20261026) with v1-b300-box-a.args + env-box-a.txt
ROLLBACK_TREES="9a9ede7ae0183e7c43956395238e29c406d85fe8 4943d6ed906ad0f761c4845ce85ad664e7f1b7fb"   # the way back, first entry first (FORK_TREE's comment)
FORK_BASE=3a3a8611a45f5a81fd07ffa6b0ed3ba33e7a4db9   # the upstream/main commit prod's tip 163591d9fc still sits on, as 9a9ede7ae0 and 4943d6ed90 did (9a9ede7ae0..163591d9fc is nine commits, no merge: sweep-c's seven cherry-picks + the two hicache-evict commits; 3a3a8611a4 an ancestor, checked in the registered checkout for #915; the picks are cherry-picks; the merge of box-a-mk-latest, qa/prod-merge-20261030/merge.md), read only by fork-sync.sh (its `git rebase --onto` anchor); box-c's box file names the same base
FORK_HOST="root@<FORK_HOST>"
FORK_CLONE=/opt/box-f-fork/sglang            # the fork host's working-clone path (matches mirror-and-branch.sh's default FORK_DIR)
FORK_DEPLOY_KEY="~/.ssh/<FORK_DEPLOY_KEY>"     # box-c's read-only deploy key, reused: this box tracks the same fork. Staged to the box, never into an onstart
# Fork mirror (mirror-and-branch.sh) and the pinned serving image (offer-search.sh, image-build.sh).
FORK_PRIVATE_REPO="<SGLANG_FORK_URL>"   # the private fork mirror's ssh clone URL: the box's `fork` remote
FORK_MIRROR=/opt/box-f-fork/sglang-mirror.git   # the fork host's bare mirror path, beside FORK_CLONE
FORK_MIRROR_BASE=main            # upstream deleted its dsv4.1 branch ~2026-09-15; main is the base left to cut from
GRAFT_SRC="<HOME>/workspace/backups/grafts/campaign-1017/graft-1017-l3a"   # l3a, box-c's graft: its directory on THIS Mac (edited_tensors.safetensors + applier.json + manifest.json), so a re-create rebuilds the same repack from its own STOCK_DIR download. Our grafts never come from Hugging Face (our internal artifact policy)
GRAFT_SHA256=5d234cfe4bf03349cfc57b7c36a7179ee0aca04e3a33c1435b91b3be225b1aa4   # the pin: sha256 of that directory's edited_tensors.safetensors (2,151,697,824 B), the graft manifest's own graft.edited_tensors_sha256
GRAFT_DIR="<GRAFT_DIR>"   # the box path the three graft files land on; graft-apply.sh rebuilds MODEL_DIR from STOCK_DIR + this
APPLY_GRAFT_PY="<APPLY_GRAFT_PY>"   # the box-side copy of the grafting kit's apply_graft.py that bringup.sh stages (sha256-checked)
CONTAINER_IMAGE=lmsysorg/sglang:dev-dsv41@sha256:4a5d132a06a77c8331e15845f2e925adc788b00105097ad55409afa3f4fa4860   # box-c's pinned dev-dsv41 digest, the image <INSTANCE_ID> runs: the container FORK_TREE runs in, out of VENV and SGLANG_TREE above
